<h2 id="scope">How Fiverr works</h2>
<p>Freelancers publish a Gig that explains the service, category, package options, delivery time, revisions, requirements and portfolio media. The official setup guide says Gig creation and editing are available on desktop. It also says sellers can offer up to three packages, while the minimum starting price is US$5 unless a category requires a higher minimum. <a href="https://help.fiverr.com/hc/en-us/articles/360010451397-Creating-a-Gig">Fiverr Gig creation guide, checked October 31, 2026.</a></p>
<p>Buyers can search and filter by budget, delivery time, language, location and other details where available. Fiverr recommends contacting a freelancer before ordering when the requirements are unclear. Some Gigs allow direct ordering; others use a request-to-order flow or a custom offer. This means the buyer should read the exact package and ask questions before paying, not infer scope from the thumbnail alone. <a href="https://help.fiverr.com/hc/en-us/articles/49421104364049-Searching-freelancers-and-services-on-Fiverr-A-Guide">Official search guide, checked October 31, 2026.</a></p>
<h2 id="features">Features that shape the decision</h2>
<h3>Packaged services and add-ons</h3><p>Basic, Standard and Premium packages let sellers describe different levels of scope. Delivery time, revision count, requirements and optional extras affect the real offer. A package comparison helps a buyer see whether the cheaper option leaves out a source file, a second version, setup support or a key revision. Sellers should state exclusions plainly so the buyer can compare offers without guessing.</p>
<h3>Search, profiles and portfolios</h3><p>Buyers can compare profiles, service descriptions, work samples and eligible reviews. The platform's search filters vary by category, so the same filter set will not appear for every service. Review the actual category page and the seller's relevant samples instead of treating one general rating as proof that the person can complete a specific brief.</p>
<h3>Order requirements and delivery</h3><p>Fiverr lets sellers collect requirements before work starts. This can reduce back-and-forth when the seller asks for the right files, access details, examples and acceptance criteria. For buyers, a complete brief is one of the best ways to reduce avoidable changes. For sellers, it helps identify a mismatch before committing to a deadline.</p>
<h3>Reviews and dispute steps</h3><p>Fiverr's review guide says clients can leave a review on a completed or eligible canceled order, and reviews must come from legitimate purchases. The Resolution Center is for issues on active orders; its official guide says the other party has 48 hours to accept or decline a request. Completed or canceled orders have different options, so read the current help page before relying on a cancellation or refund path. <a href="https://help.fiverr.com/hc/en-us/articles/360049982353-Leaving-and-managing-reviews-on-Fiverr">Review guide</a> and <a href="https://help.fiverr.com/hc/en-us/articles/37332569612049-Using-the-Resolution-Center">Resolution Center guide</a>, checked October 31, 2026.</p>
<h2 id="strengths">Where Fiverr is a good fit</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Clear deliverables:</strong> logo variations, short edits, specific development tasks, writing assignments or other work that can be scoped before purchase.</li><li><strong>Fast comparison:</strong> buyers can review several offers and sample work before deciding.</li><li><strong>Repeatable services:</strong> a seller can turn a proven task into a consistent package with clear requirements.</li><li><strong>Smaller starting projects:</strong> the buyer can begin with a defined scope before agreeing to a broader engagement, subject to category minimums and fees.</li></ul>
<h2 id="limits">Limits and risks to understand</h2>
<p>The main commercial drawback for sellers is the 20% share Fiverr keeps from each completed order. This can be manageable when the platform brings a buyer the freelancer would not otherwise reach, but it should be included in the price calculation. The buyer must also compare the final checkout total, because the service price alone may not be the amount charged.</p>
<p>The Gig format can be awkward for discovery-heavy projects. A brand strategy, long website migration or ongoing analytics program may need workshops, milestones, changing requirements and regular meetings. A packaged listing can still start the conversation, but the scope must be agreed before work begins. If the engagement is mainly hourly or changes week to week, compare proposal-based marketplaces.</p>
<p>Fiverr also does not remove the need for due diligence. Check whether the seller's examples are relevant, whether the delivery includes editable files, what counts as a revision, how a cancellation works and who owns the result under the applicable terms. No public profile or review count guarantees a particular outcome.</p>
<h2 id="pricing">Fees and pricing</h2>
<p>Fiverr is not priced like a monthly software subscription. Sellers set Gig prices, and the platform takes its share from completed orders. Its Earnings page says freelancers receive 80% of the purchase amount, including extras and tips. A US$100 order therefore produces US$80 in Fiverr earnings before taxes and any separate payout-provider or currency-conversion charges. <a href="https://help.fiverr.com/hc/en-us/articles/9234443621137-Your-earnings-page">Official earnings page, checked October 31, 2026.</a></p>
<p>For buyers, the official Help Center page on upfront pricing lists a standard service fee of 5.5% and an extra US$3.50 for orders under US$200. Fiverr also says the upfront-price display is used in selected regions, where the amount shown can include required fees. The Payment Terms page separately describes an Order Initiation Fee. Because checkout displays and legal fee wording can depend on the transaction, use the final total shown for your location. <a href="https://help.fiverr.com/hc/en-us/articles/360011562878-Price-upfront-Clear-and-predictable-pricing">Buyer fee guide</a> and <a href="https://www.fiverr.com/legal-portal/legal-terms/payment-terms-of-service">Payment Terms</a>, checked October 31, 2026.</p>
<p>Payout fees depend on the withdrawal method and location. Fiverr's official withdrawal guide lists PayPal, bank transfer through Payoneer and a Payoneer account, with different minimums, transfer times and fees. The Fiverr Revenue Card is discontinued for new users. <a href="https://help.fiverr.com/hc/en-us/articles/360010530058-Withdrawing-your-earnings-managing-payout-methods">Withdrawal guide, checked October 31, 2026.</a> Use the <a href="/fiverr/pricing/">Fiverr pricing guide</a> for a fuller breakdown.</p>
<h2 id="fit">Who should use Fiverr, and who should compare alternatives?</h2>
<p>Fiverr suits buyers who can write a precise brief and freelancers who can package a repeatable service with a clear deliverable. It is also useful when the buyer wants to compare multiple service listings before contacting a provider.</p>
<p>Compare alternatives if you need hourly contracts, complex milestones, senior expert screening, design contests, a different commission model or a portfolio-first payment workspace. The <a href="/fiverr/alternatives/">Fiverr alternatives guide</a> compares Upwork, Contra, Freelancer.com, PeoplePerHour, Guru, Toptal and 99designs by work model and official fee structure. The <a href="/compare/fiverr-vs-upwork/">Fiverr vs Upwork comparison</a> is the more focused choice when you are deciding between packaged Gigs and proposal-based contracts.</p>
<h2 id="alternatives">Alternatives to consider</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Upwork:</strong> compare it when the job needs hourly or fixed-price contracts and may continue beyond one delivery.</li><li><strong>Contra:</strong> compare it when you have a portfolio and want commission-free freelancer payments, while accounting for client platform fees.</li><li><strong>Freelancer.com:</strong> compare it when you want competing bids or a design contest.</li><li><strong>Toptal:</strong> compare it for experienced specialists and a screened talent network.</li></ul>
<h2 id="faq">Fiverr review FAQ</h2>
<h3>How much does Fiverr take from freelancers?</h3><p>Fiverr says freelancers receive 80% of the purchase amount for completed orders, including extras and tips. Separate payout-provider or currency-conversion charges may still apply.</p>
<h3>Is Fiverr free to join?</h3><p>A basic account and Gig can be started without a conventional monthly marketplace subscription, but sellers keep 80% of the purchase amount and buyers may pay service fees.</p>
<h3>Can I use Fiverr for long-term work?</h3><p>Yes, if the project scope and terms fit the platform. If the work is mainly hourly or changes frequently, compare contract-based marketplaces before choosing.</p>
<h3>Can Fiverr reviews move to another marketplace?</h3><p>No official bulk transfer route for reviews or seller levels was confirmed in the sources checked October 31, 2026. Keep permitted portfolio and financial records and rebuild the new profile under its own rules.</p>
